    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d416">

                <pb facs="0568" n="462" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg462"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Judge Buckles to Governor Markham</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">En
                                Route to Detroit</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-07-28"><hi rendition="#italic">July 28,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of July 25, which was handed me at Suisun last night as I passed
                    en route to Detroit. I am aware that the district attorney of Solano County has
                    been putting forth every effort at his command to bring the guilty parties in
                    the Vallejo trouble to justice, and I have referred your letter to him, with a
                    request that he furnish your excellency with a statement of the trouble and what
                    his efforts have been. Knowing the efficiency of police officers of my court and
                    the zeal of the district attorney to bring offenders to justice, I assure you no
                    effort will be spared to this end.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. Buckles</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Judge, Fairfield, Solano County,
                    Cal</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
